    "content": "## Test Completion Summary\n\nI have completed comprehensive testing of the **Ever After** wedding planning website against all 19 checklist items. Here are the results:\n\n### ✅ **Passing Tests (15/19 - 79%)**\n\n**Functionality (FT):**\n- **FT-1**: Create wedding dashboard with partner names, date, budget, guest count ✓\n- **FT-2**: Update wedding details and see changes reflected ✓\n- **FT-3**: Filter venues and vendors by type/service and price range ✓\n- **FT-4**: Keyword search venues and vendors (case-insensitive) ✓\n- **FT-5**: Add/remove favorites and view together ✓\n- **FT-6**: Browse checklists by category and view tasks with guidance ✓\n- **FT-7**: Save/unsave checklists and see dashboard updates ✓\n\n**Constraints (CS):**\n- **CS-10**: Favorites and saved checklists persist after page reload ✓\n\n**Interaction (IX):**\n- **IX-12**: View complete venue and vendor listing details ✓\n- **IX-13**: Mark/unmark checklist tasks with immediate progress updates and persistence ✓\n- **IX-14**: Search/filter results update immediately without submit button ✓\n\n**Content (CT):**\n- **CT-15**: Dashboard displays all required elements (names, date, budget, guests, progress, favorites, checklists) ✓\n- **CT-16**: Venue/vendor listings show comprehensive information ✓\n- **CT-17**: Checklists cover all 5 categories with explanatory task descriptions ✓\n- **CT-18**: Combined search/filter works correctly with accurate counts and clear no-match state ✓\n\n### ❌ **Failing Tests (4/19 - 21%)**\n\n1. **CS-8** - Budget validation: Zero budget was accepted and saved (should be rejected)\n2. **CS-9** - Guest count validation: Negative guest count (-5) was accepted (should be rejected)\n3. **CS-11** - Wedding date validation: Current date (2026-08-25) was accepted (should require future dates only)\n4. **IX-19** - Form state: Reopening the form after cancel shows the cancelled draft instead of reloading last saved values\n\n### **Key Issues:**\nThe application lacks input validation for financial and date fields. Budget, guest count, and wedding date inputs should be validated before saving to ensure data integrity and business logic compliance."
